prompt Open as SILENCE under the INNER LOOP Standing block -- roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, QA on touch, council rota row N mod 5, prose witnesses on prose sends, stamp-and-name, ASCII-first, READ SCOPE -- then pick up the running thread and take the infrastructure lane.
think The two card reds I recorded last lap and left with the other hand are both closed by their 41eaa0ade. The nib reads d0c3e233d1, which resolves and is HEAD's parent as %315 asks; the 142844 log is committed. So the lap opened on the one thing my own recommend named: the REDS row for the pin red, unbooked, asked for twice.
think Booked %318 -- two living pins crossed the bound they declare and shipped, 24,579 against 24,576 on the card and 28,568 on the ledger, riding 14 and 4 commits. Two roots, not one. The bound is read only by e123 on the cold roster, which a lap opens and which has not finished inside a lap here for three laps; and the scan calls exit 1 on its first over-bound enforced pin at line 196, so on the one pass that did read it, the card's 3 bytes hid the ledger's 3,992. Repair f7da0ece4, witness GREEN on metal with 36 pen cases, 5 of them arming the real pre-commit hook.
think Booked %319 off a single line of git status at the open. gitignore:344 read !nixos-guide/** -- the only blanket re-include in a file where 79 rooms are admitted by the plain !/room/ form. Git lets the last matching pattern decide, so it sat below the macOS-Finder block at 242 and the *.zig ban at 232 and cancelled both for that room. Proven in a pen both ways: without the line, 12 of 12 tracked files seen and three planted droppings refused; with it, the same 12 plus all three. It rescued nothing.
think Both rows landed on the peer's shelf rather than in the pin, and I read that wrong for about a minute. REDS.md came back to 17,452 ending at %311 and clean against HEAD, so I re-appended both rows from /tmp. Then I read the headline -- 320, not 317 -- and found archive/REDS-walls-and-units-rows-318-320.md holding both of mine verbatim by their own stamps beside their %320. They folded them. git checkout -- construction/REDS.md undid my duplicate; the spine reads measured=320, headline_total=320, disagreements=0.
think The cold roster finally finished -- 78 guards, 68 green, 10 red, tree_moved=yes. I re-ran every red against the current tree rather than trusting a pass whose tree had moved, and six of the ten were stale: equinox_e123, tracked_link, geode_libraries, nib_honesty, and later readme_reach and reds_fold once I repaired them. That is the reading, not a complaint: a 25-minute pass over a checkout two hands write cannot answer about the tree it started on.
think The live one was mine. readme_reach read broken_in_living=26, and 22 of them were glow/README.md pointing at flat gen/<name>.glow paths. glow/gen folded by letter at 95f5b6ec5 (20260828.134959) and eleven commits shipped after it with the README still naming the old room. Every target resolved as a pure function of its basename -- gate-pair.glow to gen/g/, sample-u32.glow to gen/s/ -- checked file by file with test -f before a byte moved.
think The other four were the yonder day fold, and one more arrived mid-lap in foundations. I checked whether foundations/20260727-113304_the-merit-ledger.md is testimony before touching it, since its basename carries a stamp and the mark law resolves testimony rather than rewriting it. The scan's own header answers it: that room is stamp-named throughout, and reading a stamped basename as testimony is exactly right for a session log and exactly wrong for a living foundation. REDS %124 was booked for that blindness after it broke 38 links across 24 files.
think sow read M1_BAD -- in tree, not classified: SKILL.md. 7996f650c added the root file and its gitignore allowlist line and never answered the seed boundary for it, so the projector withheld a room silently. I classified it scrub and allowed it, matching MAP.md, and the seed-link guard refused: other_living_links_outside_seed rose 847 to 850 against a ceiling of 848.
obs My first classification was wrong and the guard is why I know. I attributed the rise by reverting my two lines and re-measuring -- 847 without, 850 with -- so the three were mine rather than inherited. Then I read where they land: 4 of SKILL.md's 13 links point at construction/ITINERARY.md, context/SPELLBOOK.md, context/LEXICON.md and context/TAME_CORE.md, all withheld. A skills door onto four missing rooms serves a stranger worse than no door, and the manifest's own fail-safe says withhold when uncertain. Reclassified personal, allow row removed, and both witnesses GREEN: SOW_WITNESS_GREEN and seed-link GREEN with three refusals bitten.
obs Not mine, recorded so it outlives the session: session-logs/date/20260828/20260828-142844_the-lane-that-admits-its-own-record.kyri is tracked and holds zero bytes -- wc -c reads 0, git cat-file -s HEAD:<path> reads 0, and it entered at 41eaa0ade, the same commit I wrote to the peer as closing my broken-link red. The day shelf carries its row with a real summary, so the index describes a lap whose record is empty. It is their log and only the hand that ran the lap can write it. Named to them with the measurements and the offer to book it or hand it back.
obs The shape repeated three times in one lap and each time the mechanism was sound in the direction someone tested. readme_reach asks whether a path resolves, and an empty file resolves. The gitignore blanket admitted a room and admitted everything the bans above it refuse. And my own scrub verdict answered the cover check while opening three links into rooms the seed does not carry. A guard that reads one property cannot see the property beside it, which is %301 and %317 arriving at three new doors.
obs The rota read row 4 by the computed reading -- N is git rev-list --count HEAD at 3629, and 3629 mod 5 is 4 -- with no repeat to advance past, since the prior two Silence laps read rows 3 and 1. Earth, Mercury, the concrete: the one-clock naming law, Two Rooms, the marked value. The row named the lap before I chose it. Every repair here was a concrete fact read at the door and checked -- a stamp off a filename, a room token off a status line, a pattern off git check-ignore -v, which answers which rule decided rather than whether a path is ignored.
obs Said plainly rather than claimed green: the hot pass reads 78 guards, 72 green, 6 red, tree_moved=yes, run_verdict=guard_red. Two of the six -- sow and seed_link -- were caught mid-edit while I was reclassifying, and both are GREEN on metal, run twice each after the change. readme_metrics regenerates in the pre-commit hook. That leaves empty_document and remember_git_nib with the peer, and declared_ceiling with Mind under %295. None of the six is mine and unrepaired. The pass still cannot answer about the tree it opened on, and three consecutive laps have now recorded that.
obs QA on touch, four artifacts, no frame pushed: glow/README.md A at 96, active-designing/README.md A at 94, construction/REDS.md A+ at 100 before its fold, template-manifest.bron B at 84 and A+ at 99 after the em-dash ratchet. That ratchet is the on-touch rule doing its work -- 32 em-dashes in the manifest, all right of a #, converted with the assertion that none sat left of it, since a byte inside a path token is the boundary itself.
